      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T03:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On that note, for you going forward : you can\u0027t assume there is only one wifi network. Although it\u0027s true that many devices have some kind of hardware limit on some technology (if your wifi chip only supports one connection then sure you can only have one wifi at any given time), you can\u0027t assume you\u0027re on a device with no support for multiple wifi networks (they absolutely exist). There can be multiple networks of any technology at any given time.",
      "parentUuid": "85cf1d2b_b4f5a182",
